{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-02T21:46:04.327Z","data":{"text":"Task 4 is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nConverted `osq sync`, `osq graph`, and `osq migrate` to report failure by throwing `CommandError`, removing the injectable `exit` option and every `process.exitCode` assignment.\n\n**Source changes:**\n- `src/cli/sync.ts`, `src/cli/graph.ts`: failure now throws `CommandError(<line>)` instead of printing to stderr and setting the exit code. Success stdout/progress unchanged.\n- `src/cli/migrate.ts`: unsupported targets and failed migrations log exactly as before, then throw `new CommandError('', { exitCode: 1 })`. Success still returns its result (return type dropped `| null`).\n\n**Tests:**\n- New `tests/sync-graph-migrate-command-error.test.ts` covers the option types, each failure via `assert.rejects`, and each command through `runCliCaptured` (with a `process.stderr` tap for migrate's logger).\n- Updated `vcs-sync-command`, `web-graph-command`, `migrate`, and `migrate-sidecars` to expect the thrown `CommandError` and pass no `exit`.\n\nBoth the task verify (`node --import tsx --test tests/sync-graph-migrate-command-error.test.ts`) and the proposal verify (`pnpm verify`: typechecks, build, all tests, lint) pass. Result written to `.run/results/4.md`."}}
